  "equipment_type": "Boiler controller",
  "applies_to": "IBC SL, VFC and EX boilers with the V-10 touchscreen controller and the licensed BACnet interface option.",
  "summary": "The V-10 touchscreen controller serves BACnet IP once the BACnet option is licensed. Each boiler on the network gets its own set of temperature, pressure, flow, run-hour, load and status objects, and the boiler designated as BoilerNet master adds a small group of master objects. The BMS can write outdoor and indoor temperature, the supply setpoint, occupancy, enable, setbacks, thermostat demands, service mode and load types.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet IP"
  ],
  "firmware": null,
  "default_device_instance": null,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "The manual prints object IDs with an 'xxx' prefix (e.g. xxxAI1) for boiler 1 only and says the real IDs are site specific; each boiler has its own copy of the boiler objects. Instances here are the printed numbers.",
    "Fan Speed is printed as 'xxxA8'; it sits in the AI sequence and is listed as AI 8. The Boiler Over Temp. name is printed cut off ('oiler Over Temp.').",
    "Objects not valid for a model (e.g. outlet pressure and delta pressure on SL boilers) or for missing sensors read no usable value.",
    "Master objects only exist when a boiler is designated BoilerNet master.",
    "Commandable objects marked 1 relinquish after 5 minutes without BACnet communication; objects marked 2 change the saved controller setting and are not restored by relinquish."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "BACnet Interface (V-10 controller) configuration",
    "doc_number": null,
    "revision_date": "2024-06-04",
    "url": "https://www.ibcboiler.com/support/TIPortal/Content/Installation_&_Maintenance/Knowledge_base/PDF/BACnet%20Interface%20(V-10%20controller)%20configuration.pdf"
  },
  "integration": {
    "summary": "License the BACnet option on the V-10 and connect it to the BACnet IP network. Enable the boiler with BV 10, set occupancy with BV 9, and write the supply setpoint (AV 37) or feed outdoor temperature (AV 35); read operating status, supply and return temperatures and the error message.",
    "minimum_points": [
      {
        "ref": "BV 10",
        "name": "Boiler Enable",
        "why": "Boiler enable from the BMS"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 9",
        "name": "Occupied",
        "why": "Occupied/unoccupied command"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AV 37",
        "name": "Supply Setpoint",
        "why": "Supply water setpoint, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 1",
        "name": "Operating Status",
        "why": "Standby, purging, heating, error and so on"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 1",
        "name": "Supply Temp.",
        "why": "Supply water temperature, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "AI 2",
        "name": "Return Temp.",
        "why": "Return water temperature, °C"
      },
      {
        "ref": "BV 6",
        "name": "Comm. Status",
        "why": "Boiler communication status"
      },
      {
        "ref": "MV 2",
        "name": "Error Message",
        "why": "Active error"
      }
    ],
    "enable": "BV 10 Boiler Enable and BV 9 Occupied are commandable; both change the saved setting in the controller, so a relinquish does not restore the previous value.",
    "heartbeat": "Outdoor Temp., Indoor Temp., Supply Setpoint, Thermostat 1-4 and the master outdoor/indoor/setpoint objects return to their relinquish values after 5 minutes without BACnet communication, so the BMS must keep writing them.",
    "remote_sensors": "AV 35 Outdoor Temp. and AV 36 Indoor Temp. (and AV 1103/1104 on the master) take values from the BMS; they relinquish after 5 minutes of lost communication.",
    "setup": [
      "The BACnet interface is a licensed option (per boiler or per site).",
      "BACnet IP only; the interface does not support BBMD, foreign-device registration or BACnet routing.",
      "Object IDs are site specific; the manual's numbering scheme uses a boiler ID plus a 3-digit object ID."
    ],
    "gotchas": [
      "Objects marked note 2 (Occupied, Boiler Enable, Setback 1-4, Service Mode, Load 1-4 Type) write the saved controller setting; do not write them cyclically.",
      "Outlet Pressure and Delta Pressure are not usable on SL models.",
      "Stack and air temperature read only if those sensors are fitted."
    ]
  },
